Description: Annotates each sample of a post-mortem tissue cohort (GTEx or
    similar) with its position along three transcriptional axes of donor
    death derived from GTEx v8 across ten tissues: ventilator (perfused
    versus post-mortem), post-mortem ischemia and prolonged agony. For every
    sample it returns a signature score per axis, a position scaled between
    the two reference poles of the same tissue, the fraction of the sample's
    deviation from the tissue centroid that lies along the death axes, a
    state label and technical contamination flags. Samples can then be
    plotted, selected or excluded with explicit criteria, and the per-sample
    scores can be used as covariates in differential-expression designs or
    batch-correction tools. A second group of functions annotates an existing
    differential-expression table with the death axes its genes fall in and
    the change in log fold change expected when the control subset changes.
